    {
      "id": "4582600e-e395-4323-a9fc-0aff8a8afd96",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 417,
      "shortId": "A79ST",
      "priority": 6,
      "shortName": "the-layer-stack-becomes-the-su",
      "title": "The layer stack becomes the surface TREE — z is a path, not a band",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "**Read `docs/surface-compositor.md` §2 (\"The surface tree\"), §3, §5 and §6 first** — recovered from git 2026-08-12. The tree is the recorded design; what we shipped is a flattened approximation of it.\n\n# Current state vs the design\n\n`heca/src/chrome/layers.rs` holds a **flat `Vec<DynamicLayer>`** ordered by a `LayerBand` enum\n(`Background < Content < Floating < Overlay < Modal`) plus insertion order within a band.\n\nThe design says (§2):\n\n> **z is the position in this tree — never a stored number.** A surface's z-path is the chain of\n> sibling indices from the root to it (`[4,0]`). Ordering is lexicographic on the path, which equals\n> a pre-order traversal, which equals paint order.\n>\n> - a **child is above its parent**, so a modal is above its opener;\n> - later siblings are above earlier ones;\n> - inserting \"in the middle\" is `Vec::insert` at the right sibling index — no float fragility, no\n>   renumbering by hand.\n\n§5: *\"a modal opened from the exposé is a **child of the exposé** — it automatically sits above it\nand, being modal, becomes the new `current_index`.\"*\n\n**A band is a stored z.** §6's first invariant is *\"No hardcoded z / levels anywhere\"*, and a\nfive-variant enum every caller picks from is exactly that, one step removed.\n\n# Why it is worth doing — the bugs it removes as a class\n\nBoth layer bugs found on 2026-08-11 are \"z is stored/implicit\" bugs, not incidents:\n\n1. **`add_named` removed-and-re-appended**, so rebuilding a layer promoted it above anything opened\n   since — the confirm dialog opened over the exposé, the map rebuilt, and the click on \"Close\" went\n   to the map. Fixed by replacing in place.\n2. **Input and painting disagreed about which layer is in front**: painting sorted by band,\n   `top_modal_*` took the last one added and ignored the band. Fixed by giving input the same order.\n\nIn a tree neither is expressible: a rebuild replaces a node, and there is exactly one order.\n\n**The deciding argument is plugins**, which is what F003 is for. A plugin opens a panel; the panel\nopens a modal; the panel closes. The modal must sit above *that* panel and must go with it. In a flat\nlist that is bookkeeping every caller can get wrong; in the tree it is free.\n\n# What to build\n\n- `SurfaceId` + a tree of nodes, each with `parent` and ordered `children` (§7 sketches the target\n  API). Order = pre-order traversal; **delete `LayerBand`** and the `rank()` beside it.\n- **`current_index`** — the active context surface (§2's coarse mechanism). Opening a context sets\n  it; closing restores the previous. This is what T416 needs, and doing that task first against the\n  flat model means writing the gate twice.\n- **Occluder from real laid-out geometry** (§2), never a constant — already true of\n  `active_peek_targets`, keep it.\n- Migrate the three readers: `chrome::mod.rs`'s paint pass (`visible_back_to_front`),\n  `top_modal_*` / `dispatch_modal_pointer`, and `active_peek_targets`.\n- Keep `add_named`'s in-place replacement semantics (a re-registration keeps its **place, its\n  visibility and any animation in flight** — 2026-08-11), and the `heca.` owner-prefix namespacing.\n\n# Sequencing\n\n**Do it as part of P035 (plugin-05, the overlay host) or immediately before T416**, not after: the\noverlay host is the code that first creates parent/child overlays, and T416's coarse gate is\n`current_index`. Building either against the flat `Vec` means rewriting it when the tree lands.\n\n# Edge cases\n\n- **Bands are load-bearing today** for \"a `Modal`-band layer covers the content even if it says\n  otherwise\" (`a_modal_band_layer_covers_the_content_even_if_it_says_otherwise`). In the tree that\n  becomes \"a modal context is exclusive\", which is §2's own wording — make sure the test moves rather\n  than being deleted.\n- **A dissolving layer must not hold input** (`is_active`), and removal waits for the fade — keep\n  both, and note that the exposé's exit cannot sequence its zoom before its fade until a node's\n  lifetime follows the whole exit rather than the fade alone (found 2026-08-11).\n- Existing tests to carry over: `band_orders_front_to_back` (becomes path ordering),\n  `input_goes_to_the_front_most_band_not_the_last_one_added`,\n  `re_registering_a_layer_does_not_promote_it_above_a_newer_one`,\n  `re_showing_a_visible_layer_does_not_restart_its_zoom`.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
      "checklist": [],
