    {
      "id": "03a5c4c2-9bfd-4c8a-abe2-4ab1eb2b5875",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 421,
      "shortId": "RE2LB",
      "priority": 10,
      "shortName": "the-expos-is-laggy-with-many-p",
      "title": "The exposé is laggy with many panes — moving the cursor, and opening and closing it",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "**Antonio, driving, 2026-08-12:** *\"moving between panes is laggy, likewise opening / closing the expose with such a number of items\"* — with three workspaces holding roughly 25 panes between them.\n\n⚠️ **Instrument first. Do not optimise anything until a measurement says what is slow.** This is the lesson that cost most of 2026-08-11: three plausible speculative fixes, two of them real defects, and the app still broken until one traced run found the cause. Time the frame, the rebuild and the layout pass separately before touching either.\n\n# Candidates, in the order they are worth measuring\n\n1. **The whole layer is rebuilt on every cursor move.** `CardGrid::on_move` emits\n   `InteractionIntent::ExposeCursor`, which reaches `record_expose_cursor`\n   (`heca/src/chrome/expose.rs`). That only writes `AppState`, so it should be cheap — **but check\n   what else runs on that event**, in particular whether it reaches `after_mutation_change` and so\n   `refresh_visible_layers` (`heca/src/app/mutations.rs`), which rebuilds every visible host layer.\n   A rebuild of the map is `model()` over the whole session plus `map()` composing ~25 cards.\n   The comment there says focus deliberately does *not* trigger it; confirm that is still true of\n   this path.\n2. **`MutationKind::Config` now rebuilds visible layers too** (added 2026-08-12 so a window resize\n   re-fits the map). A resize storm — dragging a window edge — therefore rebuilds the map per\n   frame. If that is the lag while resizing, the rebuild wants coalescing to once per frame rather\n   than reverting the fix.\n3. **Layout over the whole map every frame.** `layout_layers` (`heca/src/chrome/mod.rs`) runs\n   `LayoutEngine::compute` on every visible layer's root each frame. With 25 cards, each a `Row`\n   inside a column inside a `ScrollRegion` inside a `CardGrid`, that is a large taffy tree — and\n   unlike the chrome it has no signature check to skip the work.\n4. **Open/close specifically.** Both play an animation (`set_zoom` / `set_fade_out`), so every\n   frame of them repaints the full-screen layer *and* the frosted backdrop\n   (`LayerBackdrop::Frosted` → the blur pass in `app/render.rs`). Full-screen blur per frame is the\n   obvious suspect for the open/close case being slow while a static map is not — measure that\n   pass on its own.\n\n# Where to look\n\n- `heca/src/chrome/expose.rs` — `model`, `map`, `register`\n- `heca/src/app/mutations.rs` — `refresh_visible_layers`\n- `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` — `layout_layers`, `paint_layers`\n- `heca/src/app/render.rs` — the layer pass and the frost blur\n\n# Verification (Antonio drives)\n\nA session of three workspaces and ~25 panes: `ctrl+h/l` moves the cursor with no perceptible delay,\nand `prefix+Tab` opens and closes at the same frame rate the app runs at otherwise.",
      "notes": "",
